🏢 Part 2: GitHub Enterprise API — Future Reference
 
Key Differences from Public
 
Item Public ( api.github.com ) Enterprise ( /api/v3 ) 
Base URL  https://api.github.com   https://[domain]/api/v3  
GraphQL  https://api.github.com/graphql   https://[domain]/api/graphql  
Rate Limit 5,000 req/h Configurable (default: 5,000) 
Version Rolling updates Tied to server release (e.g.,  v3.14+ ) 
Audit Log Org only Enterprise-wide available 
IP Allowlist Not available ✅ Supported 
 
Enterprise-Specific Endpoints
 
Endpoint Purpose 
 GET /api/v3/enterprises/{name}  Enterprise info 
 GET /api/v3/enterprises/{name}/stats  Usage statistics 
 GET /api/v3/enterprises/{name}/audit-log  System-wide audit 
 GET /api/v3/setup/api/health  Server health check 
 
 
 
🐍 Part 3: Code Implementation — Ready to Use
 
Python (PyGitHub)
 
python
  
from github import Github
import os

GITHUB_TOKEN = os.getenv("GITHUB_TOKEN")
GITHUB_DOMAIN = os.getenv("GITHUB_DOMAIN", "github.com")

if GITHUB_DOMAIN == "github.com":
    # ✅ Public — active now
    g = Github(GITHUB_TOKEN)
    print("🌐 Using GitHub Public API")
else:
    # 🏢 Enterprise — when deployed
    BASE_URL = f"https://{GITHUB_DOMAIN}/api/v3"
    g = Github(base_url=BASE_URL, login_or_token=GITHUB_TOKEN)
    print(f"🏢 Using Enterprise: {BASE_URL}")

# Example: List your repos
for repo in g.get_user().get_repos():
    print(f"- {repo.name}")
 
 
TypeScript (Octokit)
 
typescript
  
import { Octokit } from "@octokit/rest";

const GITHUB_TOKEN = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN;
const GITHUB_DOMAIN = process.env.GITHUB_DOMAIN || "github.com";

const octokit = new Octokit({
  auth: GITHUB_TOKEN,
  ...(GITHUB_DOMAIN !== "github.com" && {
    baseUrl: `https://${GITHUB_DOMAIN}/api/v3`
  })
});

// Example: Get repo info
const { data } = await octokit.rest.repos.get({
  owner: "ZyntroAI",
  repo: "fastapi-python-boilerplate"
});
console.log("✅ Repo:", data.full_name);
 
 
